cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Flow Workbench: browser-based flow cytometry gating, compensation and figure composition"
message: "If you use this software in published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lao
    given-names: Linjiang
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add your ORCID
    affiliation: "Lunenfeld-Tanenbaum Research Institute, Sinai Health"
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/flow-workbench"
url: "https://USERNAME.github.io/flow-workbench/"
abstract: >-
  Flow Workbench is a single-file, zero-install web application for flow
  cytometry analysis. It reads FCS 2.0, 3.0 and 3.1 files entirely in the
  browser and provides spillover compensation (from the file, edited by hand,
  or computed from single-stain controls), per-channel linear, log, arcsinh
  and logicle transforms, interactive hierarchical gating with rectangle,
  polygon, ellipse, interval and quadrant gates, population statistics with
  CSV export, and a figure composer with fixed and free-form layouts that
  exports PNG, vector SVG and PDF. Projects bundle the source FCS files with
  the complete analysis in one reopenable file.
keywords:
  - flow cytometry
  - FCS
  - gating
  - compensation
  - logicle
  - data visualization
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
